    "document": "WIKI/computer_vision.md",
    "chunk_text": "the application, for example: Pass/fail on automatic inspection applications. Match/no-match in recognition applications. Flag for further human review in medical, military, security and recognition applications.  Image-understanding systems Image-understanding systems (IUS) include three levels of abstraction as follows: low level includes image primitives such as edges, texture elements, or regions; intermediate level includes boundaries, surfaces and volumes; and high level includes objects, scenes, or events. Many of these requirements are entirely topics for further research. The representational requirements in the designing of IUS for these levels are: representation of prototypical concepts, concept organization, spatial knowledge,",
